{#
  nodeAffinity preference block for a pod that prefers one node but must still schedule if it
  is cordoned or full. Preference, never a pin: the weighted `preferred…` rule, unlike a
  `required…` one, lets the scheduler place the pod on the other node when the preferred one
  is cordoned or out of room.

  Why most callers prefer daniel-server: daniel-box carries the storage- and VIP-pinned
  workloads and runs the hotter of the two nodes, so latency-insensitive services default to
  daniel-server. A caller that prefers daniel-box, or whose placement has a reason of its own,
  says why in a comment at its call site.

  Arguments:
    hostname  the preferred node's `kubernetes.io/hostname` value (daniel-server or daniel-box)
    weight    every current caller uses 100; kept as a parameter rather than hardcoded so a
              future second-priority caller isn't blocked on editing this file
#}
{% macro node_affinity_preference(hostname, weight=100) %}
      affinity:
        nodeAffinity:
          preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
            - weight: {{ weight }}
              preference:
                matchExpressions:
                  - key: kubernetes.io/hostname
                    operator: In
                    values:
                      - {{ hostname }}
{%- endmacro %}

{#
  nodeAffinity pin for a pod that must run on one node. The `required` rule makes the pod
  unschedulable when that node is cordoned or full, which is the point: the pre-pull Job
  (`scripts/renderer/renderer_lib/prepull.py`) copies the pod placement, so a pin guarantees
  the image is pulled onto the node the pod runs on. A caller says why it pins in a comment
  at its call site.

  Arguments:
    hostname  the node `kubernetes.io/hostname` value
#}
{% macro node_affinity_required(hostname) %}
      affinity:
        nodeAffinity:
          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
            nodeSelectorTerms:
              - matchExpressions:
                  - key: kubernetes.io/hostname
                    operator: In
                    values:
                      - {{ hostname }}
{%- endmacro %}
